Show a worktree's services, their state and URLs. A URL is shown only while its
service runs and the router's container is up; nothing is fetched over HTTP.
With no router serving the URLs, it says why on stderr and shows `-` for every
URL; --json also carries the router's state. A worktree of another repository is
read from its own directory, and a path may lie inside the directory. It exits 0
whatever the state, and 1 when it couldn't read the worktree: Docker didn't
answer, Compose couldn't read it, or its treerig.toml wouldn't load.

Name the worktree by its UUID, its host, the path to its directory (./ ../ / ~)
or its slug. With no name, the worktree you are in.

Usage:
  treerig status [worktree] [flags]

Flags:
      --config string   path to treerig.toml (default: nearest above cwd, if
                        any)
  -h, --help            help for status
      --json            machine-readable output

Global Flags:
      --progress mode   how to show progress: auto (redraw on a terminal) or
                        plain (one line per change) (default "auto")
  -v, --verbose         show what treerig runs, and every detail
